From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: deewsing <deewsing@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Jun 2026 16:00:00 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] realtime.cfg: RT tuning for IQ-9075 EVK (PREEMPT/SCHED_CORE/EVTSTREAM)

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [platform-specific RT tuning]
Signed-off-by: deewsing <deewsing@qti.qualcomm.com>

Three RT-critical config changes for Cortex-A78C (IQ-9075 EVK):

1. PREEMPT_LAZY -> full PREEMPT
   PREEMPT_LAZY defers preemption of CFS tasks to the next voluntary
   schedule() call even when a higher-priority RT task is woken. This
   is visible as the 'N' flag (TIF_NEED_RESCHED_LAZY) which does NOT
   trigger immediate preemption at IRQ exit.
   Observed in t10.txt: snmpd (CFS, prio=120) ran for 672us after
   cyclictest (RT, prio=9) was woken, causing a 684us latency spike.
   CONFIG_PREEMPT=y forces preemption at IRQ exit (TIF_NEED_RESCHED).

2. SCHED_CORE disabled
   SCHED_CORE enables core-wide task selection across SMT siblings.
   Cortex-A78C has no SMT -- each core has exactly one hardware thread
   -- so SCHED_CORE provides zero benefit. With it enabled,
   pick_next_task() has a stale-cache fast path that can reuse a
   previous task pick even after a higher-priority RT task has been
   enqueued. Observed in t7.txt: up to 843us preemption delay.

3. ARM_ARCH_TIMER_EVTSTREAM disabled
   EVTSTRM fires a periodic event stream every ~100us to generate WFI
   wake events. On A78C this causes spurious WFI exits on idle CPUs,
   which spin in do_idle() for up to 147us waiting for the real
   arch_timer IRQ. Observed in t9.txt: all WFI exits on CPU0 were
   EVTSTRM-driven, adding directly to cyclictest latency.

Fixes: RT preemption delay on non-isolated CPUs (SEAPATH JIRA-1786)
Signed-off-by: deewsing <deewsing@qti.qualcomm.com>
---
 recipes-kernel/linux/linux-qcom-rt/realtime.cfg | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/recipes-kernel/linux/linux-qcom-rt/realtime.cfg b/recipes-kernel/linux/linux-qcom-rt/realtime.cfg
index bab20b5..dfb26f9 100644
--- a/recipes-kernel/linux/linux-qcom-rt/realtime.cfg
+++ b/recipes-kernel/linux/linux-qcom-rt/realtime.cfg
@@ -2,9 +2,10 @@
 CONFIG_NO_HZ_FULL=y
 CONFIG_CONTEXT_TRACKING_USER=y
 # CONFIG_CONTEXT_TRACKING_USER_FORCE is not set
-# CONFIG_PREEMPT is not set
-CONFIG_PREEMPT_LAZY=y
-CONFIG_SCHED_CORE=y
+CONFIG_PREEMPT=y
+# CONFIG_PREEMPT_LAZY is not set
+# CONFIG_SCHED_CORE is not set
+# CONFIG_ARM_ARCH_TIMER_EVTSTREAM is not set
 CONFIG_VIRT_CPU_ACCOUNTING=y
 CONFIG_VIRT_CPU_ACCOUNTING_GEN=y
 CONFIG_RCU_NOCB_CPU=y
--
2.43.0
